Article 22: Under any of the following circumstances, the insurance company shall advance rescue expenses within the liability limit of compulsory traffic accident liability insurance for motor vehicles, and has the right to seek recourse from the tortfeasor:

(1) the driver has not obtained driving qualifications or is drunk;

(2) the insured motor vehicle causes an accident during the period of being stolen or robbed;

(3) the insured intentionally causes a road traffic accident.

Where any of the circumstances listed in the preceding paragraph occurs and a road traffic accident occurs causing property loss to the victim, the insurance company shall not bear compensation liability.

