(2) The testing unit or institution, or the tester, does not possess the corresponding qualifications and conditions;
(3) The test results are obviously insufficiently supported;
(4) The tester intentionally conducts false testing;
(5) The tester should have recused themselves but did not;
(6) The test materials are false or contaminated;
(7) Other circumstances where re-testing should be conducted.

